    {
      "mode": "server",
      "documentation": "TEST SERVER. This statement declares the capability the server is going for in the OHIA November testing, and it will change as the payloads do. IMPLEMENTED TODAY: FHIR R4 (4.0.1) read, create, update and search on the types below (ExplanationOfBenefit: read and search only, see its own note), and a transaction at the base; one shared bearer token for everything except this statement; receiving a UC04a or UC07 referral and pulling its images with ARex at POST {{BASE}}/ode/receive/{uc04a|uc07}; sending a UC04a or UC07 referral to a registered tester; an ARex content server at {{BASE}}/arex (discovery {{BASE}}/arex/.well-known/smart-configuration, our client key {{BASE}}/arex/jwks.json). TARGET, NOT IMPLEMENTED YET: SMART Backend Services at the FHIR base (signed key assertions); ODE profile validation and validation feedback; ARex manifest signature verification; a transaction posted to the FHIR base itself starting the ARex image pull (today only the receive endpoint does that).",
      "security": {
        "description": "Interim: send Authorization: Bearer <shared token> on every request except GET {{BASE}}/fhir/metadata. Target: SMART Backend Services (client_credentials with a signed private_key_jwt assertion, RS384 or ES384). No OAuth token address is declared for the FHIR base because none is implemented here; the ARex token endpoint at {{BASE}}/arex/auth/token does not accept FHIR calls."
      },
